From d59c613b0f591aad1c5eda28d69515d8a274e135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:17:30 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] fingerprint: drive the A30s optical sensor's panel
 illumination

For an under-display optical sensor (ro.vendor.fingerprint.type=
udfps_optical, the A30s Egis ET715) the HAL now:
 - sets the panel mask level (/sys/class/lcd/panel/mask_brightness, 337)
   at enroll/authenticate and switches the mask layer on through the
   kernel's fingerprint_illum node only while a finger is down, then
   releases both (pointer-up, success, error, cancel, enroll done);
 - requests the optical calibration when the trustlet's calibration data
   is missing from /data/vendor/biometrics/meta, not only when
   force_calibrate is set, and no longer blocks enroll() waiting for it:
   touches are held back for at most 10 s while it runs;
 - passes a 60 s enroll timeout.
Every other sensor type keeps the stock flow.

For all sensors the auth token handed to the vendor library is zeroed
first, so its version byte is no longer stack garbage.

Ported from HyperRamzey's android_hardware_samsung (crdroid-16):
bf27aa4, c42e05d, ddf8141, ccd85dc, 7390806, d96c284, 6a5372f, 945f7f7,
0590464 and af75b1d. Changed here: the optical-only parts are skipped for
other sensor types, and cancel_on_enroll_completion keeps working.
